---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import MarketModel from '../components/MarketModel';

type ReadingTrail = {
  group: string;
  title: string;
  meta: string;
  blurb: string;
  href: string;
};

const readingTrail: ReadingTrail[] = [
  {
    group: 'George Shulman',
    title: 'Shulman Essay.docx',
    meta: 'Drive essay · 2020',
    blurb: 'A theorizing-politics essay returning to Baldwin, whiteness, blackness, and power.',
    href: 'https://drive.google.com/file/d/1IM69MjIbq7uhGmrefnDsZwcQBpVGxyqH',
  },
  {
    group: 'George Shulman',
    title: 'FNT - TP.docx',
    meta: 'Companion draft · 2020',
    blurb: 'A second draft keeping the same political knot in view from another angle.',
    href: 'https://drive.google.com/file/d/1D7MgF1-1Sg3D6rhRr6v7H6e2AIP5SfqP',
  },
  {
    group: 'Desert of the Real',
    title: 'Desert of the Real Proposal',
    meta: 'Early proposal',
    blurb: 'The first rough framing for Marx, Bartleby, and refusal as a writing path.',
    href: 'https://docs.google.com/document/d/16hLqb7IAXvXGW5VhHXiZydEc0Luqowc1_3xwjo8Vxtc',
  },
  {
    group: 'Desert of the Real',
    title: 'Intro Paragraph For Desert of the Real.docx',
    meta: 'Draft opener',
    blurb: 'The opening paragraph sketch before the essay settled into its final shape.',
    href: 'https://docs.google.com/document/d/1RlJ1Gzdh1ohEi0hTIiMjHpGXf-IvsshT',
  },
  {
    group: 'Desert of the Real',
    title: 'Essay For Desert Of The Real.docx',
    meta: 'Finished essay',
    blurb: 'The completed Marx and Bartleby essay, kept here as a steady aside beside the model.',
    href: 'https://drive.google.com/file/d/129D_8DSXKOWwACEDRzygo4ZntY-KNNwE',
  },
  {
    group: 'Marx',
    title: 'Chapter_13_Marx.pdf',
    meta: 'Primary text shelf',
    blurb: 'A source anchor for the way this page keeps reading money, labor, and refusal.',
    href: 'https://drive.google.com/file/d/19Os1NCxqjub0L3a0ZhHjiGjDsw7vIFFr',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Money & Wealth - a_e.s_"
  description="An unfolding essay on money, wealth, survival, and the diagram that helps make the difference legible."
  theme="archive"
  bodyClass="money-wealth-page"
>
  <main class="money-wealth-shell">
    <header class="money-wealth-hero">
      <div class="money-wealth-hero__copy">
        <p class="money-wealth-hero__kicker">Problem record</p>
        <h1>Money & Wealth</h1>
        <p class="money-wealth-hero__lede">
          I keep coming back to the difference between needing money to live and having wealth as stored flexibility.
          This page is me learning to understand that difference, and the diagram is the working map I keep returning
          to while I do it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="money-wealth-hero__card">
        <p class="money-wealth-hero__card-label">Working position</p>
        <p>
          Money is pressure. Wealth is time, insulation, and room to choose. If that distinction stays blurry, the
          market starts pretending it is a moral system instead of a survival system.
        </p>
      </aside>
    </header>

    <section class="money-wealth-layout">
      <div class="money-wealth-main">
        <article class="money-wealth-block">
          <p class="money-wealth-block__label">What I keep naming</p>
          <h2>Money is not the same thing as wealth</h2>
          <p>
            Money moves through life as a medium for exchange. Wealth, by contrast, stores possibility. It is the
            difference between a person who can keep choosing and a person who has to keep converting every hour into
            survival.
          </p>
          <p>
            When I name money and wealth as a problem, I am really naming the way they reorganize the rest of life:
            housing, food, time, care, mobility, education, and the right not to be constantly at the mercy of a
            market.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="money-wealth-block">
          <p class="money-wealth-block__label">Why the model exists</p>
          <h2>Some markets should not be treated like ordinary choice</h2>
          <p>
            The diagram began as a way to separate survival from desire. I needed a way to say that housing,
            food, utilities, healthcare, and transportation are not just categories in an economy. They are the floor
            people stand on before preference even becomes meaningful.
          </p>
          <p>
            That is why this page stays open instead of closing on a slogan. I am still learning how to read the line
            between what keeps a person alive, what keeps a person resourced, and what simply belongs to the lane of
            desire.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="money-wealth-model">
          <p class="money-wealth-block__label">Working diagram</p>
          <h2>The working diagram sits inside the essay</h2>
          <p>
            I do not treat the diagram as a final answer. I treat it as a working draft that helps me stay honest
            about where the survival floor begins, where the subsidy question changes shape, and where the rest of the
            economy starts asking for preference signals.
          </p>

          <div class="money-wealth-model__frame">
            <MarketModel client:only="react" />
          </div>

          <p class="money-wealth-model__note">
            The diagram stays here as part of the thought, not as decoration. It is one of the ways I keep reading
            the difference between money, wealth, and the rest of the market without pretending the question is
            finished.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="money-wealth-block money-wealth-block--closing">
          <p class="money-wealth-block__label">How the thought continues</p>
          <h2>The page stays open on purpose</h2>
          <p>
            The reading trail beside this page is not a bibliography that closes the question. It is the set of notes
            I keep returning to when I want the argument to stay alive. George Shulman keeps the political question
            active. Marx keeps the labor question active. The Desert of the Real drafts keep the refusal question
            active.
          </p>
          <p>
            I want the page to feel like a thought continuing instead of a claim being polished shut. The point is
            not to say the model is done. The point is to keep making it legible enough that I can keep learning from
            it.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <aside class="money-wealth-shelf">
        <div class="money-wealth-shelf__intro">
          <p class="money-wealth-block__label">Asides</p>
          <h2>Reading beside the model</h2>
          <p>
            These are the drafts and essays that sit next to the page while I work. They are not there to prove the
            model. They are there to keep the thinking honest.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="money-wealth-source-stack">
          {readingTrail.map((item) => (
            <article class="money-wealth-source">
              <p class="money-wealth-source__group">{item.group}</p>
              <h3>{item.title}</h3>
              <p class="money-wealth-source__meta">{item.meta}</p>
              <p class="money-wealth-source__blurb">{item.blurb}</p>
              <a href={item.href} class="money-wealth-source__link" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
                Open source
              </a>
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>
      </aside>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  :global(body.money-wealth-page[data-theme='archive']) {
    background:
      radial-gradient(40rem 26rem at 12% 0%, rgba(196, 158, 93, 0.16), transparent 72%),
      radial-gradient(30rem 20rem at 88% 8%, rgba(116, 156, 188, 0.12), transparent 76%),
      linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(247, 242, 233, 0.98), rgba(236, 228, 214, 0.98));
  }

  .money-wealth-shell {
    width: min(1240px, calc(100vw - 2rem));
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 3.2rem) 0 clamp(3rem, 6vw, 4.6rem);
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .money-wealth-hero,
  .money-wealth-block,
  .money-wealth-model,
  .money-wealth-shelf__intro,
  .money-wealth-source {
    border: 1px solid rgba(198, 180, 151, 0.68);
    background: rgba(250, 245, 238, 0.92);
    border-radius: 1.35rem;
    box-shadow: 0 18px 34px rgba(110, 89, 61, 0.08);
  }

  .money-wealth-hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.28fr) minmax(280px, 0.72fr);
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: clamp(1.2rem, 2.5vw, 1.7rem);
  }

  .money-wealth-hero__copy {
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .money-wealth-hero__kicker,
  .money-wealth-hero__card-label,
  .money-wealth-block__label,
  .money-wealth-source__group {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: rgba(181, 136, 78, 0.94);
  }

  .money-wealth-hero h1,
  .money-wealth-block h2,
  .money-wealth-shelf__intro h2,
  .money-wealth-source h3 {
    margin: 0.45rem 0 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display, serif);
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    line-height: 1.04;
    color: rgba(57, 42, 29, 0.98);
  }

  .money-wealth-hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.6rem);
  }

  .money-wealth-block h2,
  .money-wealth-shelf__intro h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 2.5vw, 1.75rem);
  }

  .money-wealth-source h3 {
    font-size: 1.18rem;
  }

  .money-wealth-hero__lede,
  .money-wealth-hero__card p,
  .money-wealth-block p,
  .money-wealth-shelf__intro p,
  .money-wealth-source__blurb,
  .money-wealth-source__meta,
  .money-wealth-model__note {
    margin: 0.8rem 0 0;
    line-height: 1.72;
    color: rgba(73, 59, 47, 0.86);
  }

  .money-wealth-hero__card {
    padding: 1rem 1.05rem;
    border-radius: 1rem;
    background: rgba(243, 234, 220, 0.8);
    border: 1px solid rgba(198, 180, 151, 0.62);
  }

  .money-wealth-layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.2fr) minmax(280px, 0.68fr);
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .money-wealth-main {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .money-wealth-block,
  .money-wealth-model {
    padding: 1.1rem 1.15rem 1.2rem;
  }

  .money-wealth-block p:last-child,
  .money-wealth-model__note,
  .money-wealth-shelf__intro p:last-child,
  .money-wealth-source__blurb {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .money-wealth-model__frame {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    padding: clamp(0.95rem, 2vw, 1.35rem);
    border-radius: 1.15rem;
    border: 1px solid rgba(198, 180, 151, 0.6);
    background: rgba(243, 234, 220, 0.74);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .money-wealth-model__note {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .money-wealth-shelf {
    position: sticky;
    top: clamp(1rem, 3vw, 1.5rem);
    align-self: start;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.9rem;
  }

  .money-wealth-shelf__intro,
  .money-wealth-source {
    padding: 1rem 1rem 1.05rem;
  }

  .money-wealth-source-stack {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.85rem;
  }

  .money-wealth-source {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.45rem;
  }

  .money-wealth-source__meta {
    margin-top: 0;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: rgba(124, 102, 82, 0.78);
  }

  .money-wealth-source__link {
    width: fit-content;
    margin-top: 0.25rem;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    color: rgba(121, 72, 28, 0.95);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(121, 72, 28, 0.24);
    transition: border-color 140ms ease, color 140ms ease;
  }

  .money-wealth-source__link:hover,
  .money-wealth-source__link:focus-visible {
    color: rgba(89, 49, 13, 1);
    border-color: rgba(89, 49, 13, 0.46);
  }

  @media (max-width: 960px) {
    .money-wealth-hero,
    .money-wealth-layout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .money-wealth-shelf {
      position: static;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .money-wealth-shell {
      width: min(100vw - 1rem, 1240px);
    }

    :global(.mm-section-grid) {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr !important;
      gap: 0.5rem 0 !important;
    }

    :global(.mm-survival-grid) {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr !important;
    }

    .money-wealth-hero,
    .money-wealth-block,
    .money-wealth-model,
    .money-wealth-shelf__intro,
    .money-wealth-source {
      border-radius: 1.15rem;
    }
  }
</style>
